3. Pass-through
- passthrough_raw = dP_CA / tau
- passthrough_DiD = (dP_CA - mean_dP_C) / tau      <- save this as `passthrough`
- Interpretation: buyers' share of the tax = d1 / (d1 + s1) in C's model. Can exceed 1 (sales tax on top of excise, markups).

4. Elasticity
- elasticity_naive = dlnQ_CA / dlnP_CA
- elasticity_DiD = (dlnQ_CA - mean_dlnQ_C) / (dlnP_CA - mean_dlnP_C)      <- save this as `elasticity`
- Take each state's log change FIRST, then average (not the log of the average).
- Each piece uses its own year pair (price years for P, pack-sales years for Q).
- Print numerators and denominators separately (useful for B2).
- q0 = Q_CA(t0Q), p0 = P_CA(t0P): California's before-tax values.

